  "result": "Perfect! All 149 tests pass \u2713\n\nI've successfully added a payments module to track invoice payments:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/errors.js**: Added two new error codes:\n   - NOT_ISSUED: Invoice must be issued or partially paid to record payment\n   - OVERPAYMENT: Payment exceeds what is still owed\n\n2. **src/payments.js**: New module with two functions:\n   - `recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`:\n     - Validates invoice status is 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (NOT_ISSUED)\n     - Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID)\n     - Validates date format (DATE_INVALID via isValidDate)\n     - Prevents overpayment (OVERPAYMENT if amount > balance due)\n     - Adds payment to invoice.payments array (creates if missing)\n     - Updates status: 'paid' when fully paid, 'partially_paid' when partially paid\n     - Does not mutate original invoice\n   \n   - `balanceDue(invoice)`:\n     - Returns the invoice total minus all recorded payments\n     - Returns 0 if fully paid, clamped at 0 minimum\n\n3. **test/payments.test.js**: 18 comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Balance calculations with/without payments\n   - Status transitions ('issued' \u2192 'partially_paid' \u2192 'paid')\n   - All error cases (NOT_ISSUED, AMOUNT_INVALID, DATE_INVALID, OVERPAYMENT)\n   - Multiple payment accumulation\n   - Payment on already-partially-paid invoices\n   - Invoice immutability\n   - Edge cases (exact balance, multiple partial payments)\n\nThe payment system tracks the full audit trail of payments and correctly manages invoice status through the payment lifecycle.",
